fact WorkItem(id: "WI-668", description: some(value: "Migrate the resolver's transient goal carrier Candidate::Continuation from Vec<TermId> to Vec<Value> (design docs/design/abstract-interpreter-and-rules.md Section 10 Q1; proposal 033 Q4 \"TermId / Value asymmetry\").\n\nTODAY: Candidate::Continuation(Vec<TermId>) (kb/resolve.rs ~250) stores transit-interned TermId goals; the consumer immediately lifts them to Value::Term goals (resolve.rs ~2084, `new_goals.extend(body.into_iter().map(Value::term))`) before pushing the continuation frame. Three producers mint it: push_choice (proposal 033 / WI-075, resolve.rs ~866-867), branch-from-streams disjunction (resolve.rs ~1506), and the WI-580 body-unfold (resolve.rs ~5583, unfold_eq_operand).\n\nCHANGE: make the variant carry Vec<Value>; wrap at the producers instead of at the consumer. push_choice and branch-from-streams genuinely start from TermId goals -> wrap with Value::term at those sites; the consumer becomes `new_goals.extend(body)`.\n\nPAYOFF (why this is a WI-580 prerequisite): the WI-580 unfold pays a bridge tax for the TermId carrier. Because a Continuation's goals become Value::Term but is_unreduced_op_call is Value::Node-only, a hoisted recursive op-call is round-tripped back to a node occurrence via op_call_as_occ / term_body_to_nodes so it re-triggers the next one-step unfold. A Vec<Value> carrier lets the unfold emit native Value::Node op-call goals and DROP that bridge. Aligns with the carrier-neutral goal pipeline (WI-621) and the no-Value-to-TermId boundary (WI-348) -- both delivered, but both left this transient runtime carrier untouched.\n\nNOT covered by WI-246 (delivered): WI-246 migrated STORED rule-body atoms (RuleEntry.body: Vec<TermId> -> body_nodes occurrences) -- a persistent KB-storage layer, distinct from the resolver's runtime choice-point carrier here.\n\nACCEPTANCE: cargo-test green; Candidate::Continuation carries Vec<Value>; the WI-580 unfold's Value::Term -> node-occurrence re-materialization bridge (op_call_as_occ / term_body_to_nodes for the hoist re-trigger) removed or reduced.\n\nPREREQUISITE FOR WI-580: unblocks WI-580's remaining bridge cleanup. WI-580's body-derivation core (append structural-unfold + member eq-vs-unification) is already delivered; this migration is what lets the unfold shed its TermId round-trip."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-07-09T10:06:24Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-668", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED (2026-07-09), full anthill-core suite green, /code-review high done, committed 8cddb28f. Candidate::Continuation migrated Vec<TermId> -> Vec<Value>: term-lowered producers (push_choice, branch-from-streams) wrap Value::term, consumer is a bare extend(body). The WI-580 body-unfold now emits its hoisted op-call goals as Value::Node occurrences (materialize_from_handle at production), so the relational recursion re-triggers via op_call_as_occ's Node arm instead of round-tripping a Value::Term through term_body_to_nodes at re-entry; op_call_as_occ tightens to &self.\n\nSCOPE REFINEMENT (code review -- both correctness finders + the cross-file tracer agreed): the Term arm of op_call_as_occ is KEPT, not removed. Deleting it silently regresses any Term-carried SemEq goal with an unground bodied op-call operand -- a direct resolve(&[eq(append(?a,[3]),[1,3])]) query, or an or/push_choice branch -- because walk_view yields Value::term for any Term::Fn; that path residualizes instead of solving (a completeness loss / silent skip the repo forbids). It was untested before because every relational test wraps the eq in a rule (-> Value::Node). New regression guard wi668_term_carried_opcall_eq_case_splits queries the equation directly as a term and asserts ?a = [1] (fails with the Term arm gone, passes with it). So the Term-carrier bridge is REDUCED (WI-580 recursion routed off it) not REMOVED (it stays as the general handler for term-lowered goals) -- within the ticket's \"removed or reduced\" acceptance.\n\nCleanups: term_body_to_nodes(&[id]).into_iter().next() -> materialize_from_handle at both op_call_as_occ and the hoist producer (drops a throwaway 1-elem Vec + a misleading silent-? decline). KNOWN-BOUNDED: anf_flatten still builds the hoists as Vec<TermId> (materialized to Node here); a fully native occurrence-building unfold with no term intermediary is a separate future cleanup. Unblocks WI-580's remaining work.", at: "2026-07-09T10:06:23Z")
